// =============================================================================
// COMPLETE reference architecture — the canonical "end-to-end platform" shape.
//
// This is JSONC (JSON + // comments) for YOU, the agent, to read and understand
// the layout. When you write the project's `architecture.md`, emit PLAIN JSON
// (no comments) inside a ```json fence — strip these comments.
//
// NESTED STRUCTURE, NOT PIXELS (reference/layout.md). The tab is a tree: each container
// lays out its own children, and the renderer computes every position and size.
//   • The top level is a row: the sources group, then the platform box.
//   • The sources group is a column of four source tiles, `equal: "w"`.
//   • The platform box is a row of two children: the platform stack (a column) and the
//     Genie One tile (`track` `t1`). The wordmark and governance bar are children of that stack.
//   • The platform stack is a column, top to bottom: the db-platform wordmark, the SQL
//     lakehouse, a flow row, the Lakebase tile, then the governance bar.
//   • The flow row is a row: the Lakeflow + Genie block, then a column of the three
//     consumers (dashboard, apps, Genie Agent).
//   • `track: "t1"` on the Lakeflow block, the Genie Agent and Genie One lines them up, so the
//     path to the business user is one straight line.
//   • Edges: `from`/`to` by node id. The `@handle` is inferred from geometry (left → right
//     gives `@r` → `@l`). Name the ingest port on the target handle (see below).
//
// LEFT → RIGHT story:
//   sources → Lakeflow + Genie (one block) → lakehouse + lakebase
//        → dashboard + Genie Agent + app → Genie One (business user built in)
//   The db-platform wordmark sits at the top of the platform stack and the governance block
//   at the bottom. One big white `box` wraps the Databricks components while external
//   sources stay outside the platform boundary.
//
// THE lakeflow-genie-block HAS THREE LEFT PORTS — the edge's target handle picks one:
//   @in-lakeflow-connect  (databases / SaaS: Postgres, SAP…)
//   @in-zerobus           (realtime / sensors / events — particle-stream flow)
//   @in-direct            (files: PDF, CSV/Parquet dumps — travelling-docs flow)
//   Right port `@r` → the compute layer. Inside the block = Genie Code + SDP
//   (all bronze→silver→gold) — do NOT add separate sdp / genie-code nodes.
//
// TABS: the top level is a JSON ARRAY — each element is one tab (its `name` is
// the tab label). This file has one: the full end-to-end platform flow. (Emit
// more tabs in the array when a diagram needs multiple views.)
// =============================================================================
[
  {
    "name": "Data + AI Platform — End-to-End Architecture",
    "story": "External ERP, Postgres, and sensor systems enter a governed Databricks platform through Lakeflow; governed data then powers the dashboard, Genie, and business app. Detailed governance-control mappings belong in a governance detail tab.",
    "aspect": "16:9",
    "theme": "slide",
    "direction": "horizontal",
    "frame": {"title":"Data + AI platform, end to end","subtitle":"Lakeflow ingest → governed lakehouse → dashboard, Genie, app"},
    "options": {"trademarkLogos":true},
    "layout": "row",
    "gap": 78,
    "align": "center",
    "nodes": [
      {"id": "sources", "type": "group", "layout": "column", "gap": 60, "align": "center", "children": [
        {"id": "src-erp", "type": "source", "label": "ERP System", "icon": "file:vendor/sap"},
        {"id": "src-postgres", "type": "source", "label": "Postgres", "icon": "file:vendor/postgresql"},
        {"id": "src-sensors", "type": "source", "label": "Sensor data", "icon": "sensorSource"},
        {"id": "src-docs", "type": "source", "label": "PDF docs", "icon": "pdfLogo"}
      ] },
      {"id": "platform-box", "type": "box", "z": -1, "layout": "row", "gap": 49, "align": "center", "pad": 40, "children": [
        {"id": "platform-stack", "type": "group", "layout": "column", "gap": 23, "align": "start", "children": [
          {"id": "db-platform", "type": "db-platform"},
          {"id": "sql-lakehouse", "type": "sql-lakehouse"},
          {"id": "flow", "type": "group", "layout": "row", "gap": 78, "align": "center", "children": [
            {"id": "lakeflow-genie-block", "type": "lakeflow-genie-block", "track": "line-lakeflow-genie-block"},
            {"id": "consumers", "type": "group", "layout": "column", "gap": 60, "align": "center", "children": [
              {"id": "ai-bi-dashboard", "type": "ai-bi-dashboard"},
              {"id": "databricks-apps-work", "type": "databricks-apps-work"},
              {"id": "genie", "type": "genie", "track": "line-lakeflow-genie-block"}
            ] }
          ] },
          {"id": "lakebase", "type": "lakebase"},
          {"id": "governance-block", "type": "governance-block"}
        ] },
        {"id": "genie-one", "type": "genie-one", "rot": 90, "track": "line-lakeflow-genie-block"}
      ] }
    ],
    "edges": [
      {"id": "e1", "from": "src-erp", "to": "lakeflow-genie-block@in-lakeflow-connect", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e2", "from": "src-postgres", "to": "lakeflow-genie-block@in-lakeflow-connect", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e3", "from": "src-sensors", "to": "lakeflow-genie-block@in-zerobus", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e3b", "from": "src-docs", "to": "lakeflow-genie-block@in-direct", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e4", "from": "lakeflow-genie-block", "to": "sql-lakehouse", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e5", "from": "lakeflow-genie-block", "to": "lakebase", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e6", "from": "sql-lakehouse", "to": "ai-bi-dashboard", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e7", "from": "sql-lakehouse", "to": "genie", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e8", "from": "lakebase", "to": "databricks-apps-work", "flow": true},
      {"id": "e9", "from": "genie@t", "to": "databricks-apps-work@b"},
      {"id": "e10", "from": "ai-bi-dashboard@b", "to": "databricks-apps-work@t"},
      {"id": "e12", "from": "genie-one", "to": "genie"},
      {"id": "e13", "from": "genie-one", "to": "ai-bi-dashboard"},
      {"id": "e14", "from": "genie-one", "to": "databricks-apps-work"}
    ]
  }
]
